Genealogy of Jesus
This is the record of Jesus Christ's family line: Jesus was descended from David, who was descended from Abraham.
Ibrahim is Isaac's father. Isaac is Jacob's father. Jacob is Judah and his brothers' father.
Judah fathered Perez and Zerah, whose mother was Tamar. Perez fathered Hezron. Hezron fathered Ram.
Aram was the father of Amminadab; Amminadab was the father of Nahshon; Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Salmon son of Boaz, whose mother was Rahab. Boaz father of Obed, whose mother was Ruth. Obed father of Jesse.
Jesse was King David's father. David was Solomon's father, whose mother was Uriah's wife.
Solomon fathered Rehoboam. Rehoboam fathered Abijah. Abijah fathered Asa.
Asa was the father of Jehoshaphat. Jehoshaphat was the father of Joram. Joram was the father of Uzziah.
Uzziah fathered Jotham; Jotham fathered Ahaz; Ahaz fathered Hezekiah.
Hezekiah father of Manasseh. Manasseh father of Amon. Amon father of Josiah.
Josiah father of Jeconiah #Jeconiah 11:1 Another name for Jehoiachin And his brothers This is until the time when the Israelites were taken captive to Babylon
After being taken captive to Babylon: Jeconiah fathered Shealtiel. Shealtiel fathered Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel was the father of Abihud. Abihud was the father of Eliakim. Eliakim was the father of Azor.
Azor fathered Sadoc. Sadoc fathered Achim. Achim fathered Eliud.
Eliud is the father of Eleazar. Eleazar is the father of Matan. Matan is the father of Jacob.
Jacob Abu Youssef, Mary's husband. And Mary is Jesus' mother who is called "The Messiah."
There were fourteen generations in all from Abraham to David, seven from David to the exile in Babylon, and seven more from the exile to the Messiah. This is how Jesus Christ was born.
This is how Jesus Christ was born: His mother Mary was engaged to a man named Joseph. But before they were married, she learned that she was pregnant by the power of the Holy Spirit.
But Youssef was a good man and didn't want to expose her secret, so he decided to leave her quietly.
While Joseph was thinking about this, an angel appeared to him in a dream and said, "Joseph son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary home as your wife because what is conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."
She will give birth to a son, and you shall name him Jesus, because he will save his people from their sins.”
This happened so that what the Lord said through his prophet would come true.
"Behold, the virgin shall conceive and bear a son, and they shall call his name Immanuel (which means, God with us)."
When Joseph woke up from his sleep, he did everything that the angel of the Lord had commanded him to do; so he took his wife home with him.
But he didn't know her until she gave birth to the child whom she named "Jesus."
Wisemen from the East
When Jesus was born in Bethlehem in Judea during King Herod's reign, some wise men came from the east to Jerusalem.
They asked, "Where is the child who has been born king of the Jews? For we observed his star at its rising, and have come to pay him homage."
King Herod was disturbed when he heard this, as well as all those living in Jerusalem.
Herod gathered all the chief priests and teachers of the law to ask them where Christ was born.
They said to him, "In Bethlehem in Judea, because this is what was written by the prophet:
"But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, though you are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come for me one who will be ruler over Israel, whose origins are from of old, from ancient times."
Herod summoned the wise men secretly and asked them about the exact time when they had seen the star
Then he sent them to Bethlehem and said, "Go and search carefully for the child. When you find him, come back and tell me so I can go worship him too."
Then when they had heard the king, they departed; and, lo, the star that they had seen in the east went before them, till it came to rest over the place where the child was.
They were overjoyed when they saw the star.
They entered the house and saw the child with his mother Mary, so they bowed down to worship him. Then they opened their treasure chests and presented gifts to him: gold, frankincense, and myrrh.
Then God warned them in a dream against going back to Herod, so they traveled home by another route. The flight to Egypt
After the wise men had left, an angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream and said, "Get up! Take the child and his mother and escape to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you, for Herod is going to search for the child to kill him."
Joseph got up and took the child and his mother during the night and went to Egypt.
He remained there until Herod's death. This happened to fulfill what was spoken by the Lord through the prophet: "Out of Egypt I called my son." #From ... my son. 15:2 From Hosea 11:1. Herod kills children in Bethlehem
When Herod realized that the wise men had tricked him, he was furious and ordered all boys in Bethlehem and its surrounding areas who were two years old or younger to be killed, according to the time frame confirmed by the wise men.
Then what was said through Jeremiah the prophet came true:
A voice was heard in Ramah, weeping and great mourning, Rachel weeping for her children and refusing to be comforted because they are no more. - Return from Egypt
After Herod's death, an angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in Egypt in a dream.
He said to him, "Take the boy and his mother and go back to Israel, because those who were trying to kill the child have died."
So Joseph got up and took the child and his mother and went to the land of Israel.
But when he heard that Archelaus was reigning over Judea in place of his father Herod, he was afraid to go there. And being warned by God in a dream, he departed for the region of Galilee.
He lived in a town called Nazareth. This happened so that what was said by the prophets would be fulfilled - that Christ would be called a Nazarene. #Nazarene. 23:2 Refers to the city of Nazareth. It's also a word that resembles the Hebrew word for "branch" found in Isaiah 11:1 referring to the promise of Christ coming from David's lineage.
John the Baptist
في الوقت ده ظهر يوحنا المعمدان عشان يعظ في صحرا يهوذا.
And he said, "Repent, for the kingdom of heaven is at hand."
John this is the one about whom Isaiah prophesied when he said: "The voice of one crying in the wilderness: 'Prepare the way of the Lord, make his paths straight.'"
John wore clothing made from camel's hair, with a leather belt around his waist, and he ate locusts and wild honey.
At that time, people came from all over Judea and Jerusalem and from all around the Jordan River to hear him.
He baptized them in the Jordan River after they confessed their sins.
When John saw many Pharisees and Sadducees coming to be baptized, he said to them, "You brood of vipers! Who warned you to flee from the wrath to come?"
Produce fruit in keeping with repentance.
And do not boast by saying, "Abraham is our father." For I say to you that God is able to raise up children for Abraham from these stones.
Here is the axe placed at the roots of the trees. It will cut down every tree that does not bear good fruit, and it will be thrown into the fire.
I baptize you with water for repentance, but he who comes after me is mightier than I, whose sandals I am not worthy to carry. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and fire.
He will carry his notebooks in his hand and clean his barnyard, gather his grains in the granary, and burn the hay with an unquenchable fire." Baptism of Jesus
Then Jesus came from Galilee to John at the Jordan, to be baptized by him.
But John tried to stop him, saying, "I need to be baptized by you, and do you come to me?"
But Jesus answered him, "Let it be so now; for thus it is fitting for us to fulfill all righteousness." Then he consented.
Then Jesus came from Galilee to John at the Jordan to be baptized by him. But John tried to prevent Him, saying, "I need to be baptized by You, and do you come to me?" But Jesus answered him, "Let it be so now; for thus it is fitting for us to fulfill all righteousness." Then he consented. And when He was baptized, immediately He went up from the water, and behold, the heavens were opened to him, and he saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove and coming upon Him.
And there came a voice from heaven saying, "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased."
Jesus's experience
The Spirit led Jesus into the wilderness to be tempted by the devil.
After Jesus had fasted forty days and forty nights, he was hungry.
Then the devil came to him #TheTester 3:4 that is Satan And he said to him: "If you are God's son, tell these stones to become loaves of bread."
But Jesus answered him, "It is written, 'Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that comes from the mouth of God.'"
Then Satan took him to the holy city and set him on top of the temple.
He said to him, "If you really are God's Son, throw yourself down from here. For it is written: 'He will command his angels concerning you, and they will lift you up in their hands so that you will not strike your foot against a stone.'"
Jesus replied, "It is also written: 'Do not put the Lord your God to the test.'"
Then Satan took him to a high mountain and showed him all the kingdoms of the world and their splendor.
Then he said to him: "I'll give you all this if you prostrate yourself before me."
Jesus said to him, "Get behind me, Satan! For it is written: 'Worship the Lord your God, and serve him only.'"
Then Satan left him, and angels came to serve him. Jesus began his ministry in Galilee.
When Jesus heard that John had been arrested, he withdrew to Galilee.
But he didn't stay in Nazareth; instead, he went and lived in Capernaum by Lake Galilee, in the regions of Zebulun and Naphtali.
This happened to fulfill what God said through Isaiah the prophet:
The land of Zebulun and Naphtali, along the sea coast, beyond the Jordan River, Galilee of the Gentiles.
The people who lived in darkness have seen a great light; those who dwelt in a land of deep darkness, on them has light shone.
From that time Jesus began to preach, saying, "Repent, for the kingdom of heaven is at hand." Jesus chose some disciples.
As Jesus was walking along the shore of Lake Galilee, he saw two brothers, Simon who is also called Peter, and his brother Andrew casting their nets in the lake, for they were fishermen.
He said to them, "Follow me and I will make you fishers of men."
They immediately closed their windows and followed him.
Then Jesus left there and went to another town. He saw two other brothers, James son of Zebedee and his brother John. They were in their boat with their father Zebedee mending their nets. So he called them.
They left their boat and father immediately to follow him. Jesus was teaching and healing
And Jesus went throughout all Galilee, teaching in their synagogues and proclaiming the gospel of the kingdom and healing every disease and sickness among the people.
The news about him spread throughout all Syrian lands, so they brought to Him all those who were sick with various diseases and pains, possessed by demons, epileptics, and paralytics; and He healed them.
Large crowds followed him from Galilee, from the ten cities, from Jerusalem, from Judea, and from beyond the Jordan River.
Jesus' teachings
When Jesus saw the crowds, he went up to the mountain; and after he had sat down, his disciples came to him.
And he began to speak and teach them, saying:
Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.
Blessed are those who mourn, for they will be comforted.
Blessed are the meek, for they shall inherit the earth. #They will inherit the earth. 5:5 See Psalm 37:11. It may mean here future spiritual inheritance.
Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness, for they shall be satisfied. 6:5 Literally: "To the righteous." Because God will satisfy them.
Blessed are those who show mercy, for they will be shown mercy by God.
Congratulations to those with pure hearts, for they will see God.
Congratulations to those who work for peace, because they will be called children of God.
Blessed are those who have been persecuted for righteousness' sake, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.
Congratulations when people insult you, persecute you, and falsely say all kinds of evil against you because of me.
Rejoice and be glad, for your reward is great in heaven. For they persecuted the prophets who were before you also. You are the salt of the earth; but if the salt has lost its flavor, how shall it be seasoned? It is then good for nothing but to be thrown out and trampled underfoot by men.
You are salt for all people; but if the salt has lost its flavor, how shall it be seasoned? It is then good for nothing but to be thrown out and trampled underfoot by men.
