People don't light a lamp and put it under a bowl - they put it on its stand so that it gives light to everyone in the house.
"In the same way, let your light shine before others, so that they may see your good works and give glory to your Father who is in heaven." Jesus and Moses' Law
Do not think that I came to abolish the law or the prophets; I did not come to abolish them but to fulfill them.
I tell you the truth, until heaven and earth disappear, not one dot or comma will be lost from the law until everything is accomplished.
Therefore, whoever breaks one of these least commandments and teaches others to do so will be called least in the kingdom of heaven; but whoever keeps them and teaches others to keep them will be called great in the kingdom of heaven.
For I tell you that unless your righteousness surpasses that of the Pharisees and the teachers of the law, you will certainly not enter the kingdom of heaven. Anger
You know that it was said to your ancestors: "Do not kill." #Do not kill. Exodus 20:13, Deuteronomy 5:17. And whoever kills deserves punishment.
But I say to you that anyone who is angry with his brother will be subject to judgment. Anyone who says to his brother, "Raca," is answerable to the Sanhedrin. But anyone who says, "You fool!" will be in danger of hellfire.
So if you bring your offering to the altar and there remember that someone has something against you, leave your gift there in front of the altar. Go first and make peace with that person; then come back and present your offering.
So leave your offering there in front of the altar and go make peace with that person first, then come back and present your offering.
Settle your case quickly while you're walking with him to court. Otherwise he will hand you over to the judge, who will hand you over to the jailer, who will throw you in prison.
I'm telling you the truth, you won't get out of there until you pay off your last penny. Prostitution
Have you heard that it was said: "Do not commit adultery." #Do not commit adultery. 27:5 From Exodus 20:14 and Deuteronomy 5:18.
But I say to you that whoever looks at a woman lustfully has already committed adultery with her in his heart.
Therefore if your right eye causes you to sin, pluck it out and cast it from you; for it is better that you lose one of your members than that your whole body should be cast into hell.
If your right hand is leading you to sin, cut it off and throw it away from you. It's better for one part of your body to be lost than for your whole body to go to hell. Divorce
It was also said: "If anyone divorces his wife, let him give her a certificate of divorce." # If he divorces... that. Deuteronomy 24:1
But I tell you that anyone who divorces his wife, except for sexual immorality, makes her the victim of adultery. And whoever marries a divorced woman commits adultery.
"Have you heard that it was also said to your ancestors: 'Do not swear falsely by God's name; rather, fulfill what you have sworn to do for the Lord.' #Do not break your oath...to the Lord." - Leviticus 19:12, Numbers 30:2, Deuteronomy 23:21
But I tell you this: Don't swear at all.
Do not swear by heaven because it is God's throne, nor by earth because it is His footstool, nor by Jerusalem because it is the city of the great King.
Do not swear by your head, for you cannot make one hair black or white.
If you want to say "yes," then say "yes." And if you want to say "no," then say "no." Anything beyond that is from Satan. #Satanic. 37:5 The Devil. Resistance against evil
Have you heard that it was said: "An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth." #The Eye... for a Tooth. Exodus 21:24, Leviticus 24:20
But I say to you, do not resist an evil person; but whoever slaps you on your right cheek, turn the other to him also.
If someone wants to sue you for your shirt, let them take your coat too.
If someone forces you to walk with them for one mile, then go two miles with them.
If someone asks you for something, give it to them. Don't refuse to lend money to those who ask you to borrow. Love everyone
Have you heard that it was said: "Love your neighbor and hate your enemy." #love ... your enemy. Leviticus 19:18.
But I tell you, love your enemies and pray for those who persecute you.
That is why you will be children of your Father in heaven. For God makes his sun rise on the evil and on the good, and sends rain on the just and on the unjust.
If you love those who love you only, what reward will you get? Are tax collectors not doing the same?
If you only help your brothers, what makes you different from others? Don't even idol worshippers do that too?
Therefore be perfect, just as your heavenly Father is perfect.
The bid
Be careful not to do your charitable deeds in front of people so that they will see you; otherwise, your Father who is in heaven will not reward you.
When you give to someone in need, don't announce it like blowing a trumpet for people to praise you in public places. I tell you the truth, they have already received their full reward.
But when you give to someone in need, don't let your left hand know what your right hand is doing.
Let your giving be in secret. And your Father who sees what is done in secret will reward you. Prayer
And when you pray, do not be like the hypocrites; for they love to stand and pray in the synagogues and at the street corners, that they may be seen by men. Truly I say to you, they have their reward.
But when you pray, go into your room, close the door and pray to your Father who is unseen. Then your Father, who sees what is done in secret, will reward you.
And when you pray, do not babble like pagans, who think that they will be heard because of their many words.
So don't be like them, because your Father knows what you need before you ask him for it.
Therefore pray like this: "Our Father in heaven, may your name be hallowed."
Your kingdom come, your will be done, here on earth as it is in heaven.
Give us this day our daily bread.
Forgive us our sins, just as we also forgive those who sin against us.
And do not lead us into temptation, but deliver us from evil. #The Evil One 13:6 The Devil (Satan). For Yours is the kingdom and the power and the glory forever. Amen
For if you forgive other people when they sin against you, your heavenly Father will also forgive you.
But if you don't forgive others for their mistakes, your father won't forgive yours either. Fasting
And when you fast, do not look gloomy like the hypocrites, for they disfigure their faces that people may know that they are fasting. Truly I say to you, they have received their reward in full.
But when you fast, put oil on your head and wash your face.
So that people don't notice you're fasting. But your unseen father sees it. Then your father who sees what happens in secret will reward you. Is it God or money?
Do not store treasures for yourselves on earth, where moths and rust destroy, and where thieves break in and steal.
But store up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where moths and vermin do not destroy, and where thieves do not break in and steal.
For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.
The lamp of the body is the eye. If your eyes are healthy, then your whole body will be full of light.
But if your eye is evil, then your whole body will also be full of darkness. If what is in you is light but really darkness, how much more so when it is darkness?
No one can serve two masters. Either you will hate the one and love the other, or you will be devoted to the one and despise the other. You cannot serve both God and money. #Wealth 24:6 Literally "mammon." It's an Aramaic word meaning "wealth," in its negative sense, representing here a god that people serve instead of God. The kingdom of God first
That's why I tell you, don't worry about your life, what you will eat or drink; nor for your body, what you will wear. For life is more than food, and the body is more than clothes.
Look at the birds in the sky; they do not sow or reap or gather into barns, and yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not more valuable than they?
Who among you can add an hour to their life when they worry?
Why do you worry about what to wear? Look at how the flowers in the field grow. They don't work or spin threads.
But I tell you that one of these women is greater than Solomon in all his splendor.
If God clothes the grass of the fields that you see here today, and tomorrow it is thrown into the oven, will He not care for you much more, O men of little faith?
So don't worry about these things, saying, 'What will we eat? What will we drink? What will we wear?'
These are things that people in this world strive for, but your heavenly Father knows you need them all.
But first seek his kingdom and his righteousness, and all these things will be given to you as well.
Do not worry about tomorrow; each day has enough trouble of its own. Tomorrow will have its own troubles.
Judging others
Do not judge others, so that God will not judge you.
For he will judge you by the standard that you use in judging others; and by the measure that you use it will be measured to you.
Why do you see the speck that is in your brother's eye, but fail to notice the beam that is in your own eye?
How can you say to your brother, "Let me take the speck out of your eye," when all the time there is a plank in your own eye?
Hypocrite! First remove the plank from your own eye, and then you will see clearly to remove the speck from your brother's eye.
Do not give what is holy to dogs; nor cast your pearls before swine, lest they trample them under their feet, and turn and tear you in pieces.
Ask and you will receive; seek and you will find; knock and it will be opened to you.
For everyone who asks receives; and he who seeks finds; and to him who knocks, it will be opened.
If your son asks for bread, would you give him a stone?
Or if he asks for fish, will they give him one that's alive?
Even you wicked people know how to give good gifts to your children. Won't your heavenly Father be even more willing to give good things to those who ask him? The Golden Rule
"So treat others in the way you would like to be treated. This is the essence of Moses' law and the teachings of the prophets. The path to heaven and the path to hell."
Enter through the narrow gate; for wide is the gate and broad is the way that leads to destruction, and there are many who go in by it.
But the gate is narrow that leads to life, and there are few who find it. Beware of false teachings.
Beware of false prophets who come to you in sheep's clothing but inwardly are ravenous wolves.
By their fruits you shall know them. Men do not gather grapes from thorns, nor figs from thistles!
Likewise, every good tree bears good fruit, but a bad tree bears bad fruit.
A good tree cannot bear bad fruit, nor can a bad tree bear good fruit.
And every tree that does not produce good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire.
That's why you will know false prophets by their fruit.
Not everyone who says to me, 'Lord, Lord,' will enter the kingdom of heaven, but only the one who does the will of my Father who is in heaven.
Many will say to me in that day, Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied in thy name? and in thy name have cast out devils? and in thy name done many wonderful works?
Then I shall say to them quite plainly: "I have never known you; depart from me, ye workers of iniquity." The wise man and the fool
Anyone who listens to these teachings of mine and follows them is like a wise man who built his house on rock.
The rain came down, the streams rose up, and the winds blew and beat against that house; and it fell not, for it was founded on the rock.
And everyone who hears these words of mine and does not put them into practice is like a foolish man who built his house on sand.
Then it rained, and the flood waters rose, and the wind blew and struck that house, so it collapsed in one great crash!
When Jesus had finished saying these things, the people were amazed at his teaching.
Because he taught them with authority, unlike the teachers of religious law.
Jesus cleanses a leper
Then Jesus came down from the mountain area, followed by many people.
A leper came to him and knelt down in front of him. He said, "Lord, if you want to, you can make me clean."
Then Jesus reached out his hand and touched him. "I do want to," he said. "Be clean!" Immediately the leprosy left him and he was cured.
Then Jesus said to him, "Don't tell anyone what happened, but go show yourself to the priest and offer the sacrifice that Moses commanded for your cleansing, so that they may know that you have been healed." Faith of a Roman Centurion
And Jesus entered Capernaum, where a centurion came to him, asking for help with his servant who was sick.
He said: "Sir, my servant is seriously ill and bedridden at home. He's completely immobile and suffering from severe pain."
Jesus said to him, "I will go and heal him."
The officer replied: "Sir, I'm unworthy to have you in my house; all you need is to say a word and my servant will be healed."
"I myself am under authority; I have soldiers who do what I tell them to do. I say to one soldier, 'Go!' And he goes. To another, 'Come here!' And he comes. To my servant, 'Do this!' And he does it."
When Jesus heard this, he was amazed and said to those who were following him, "I tell you the truth, I have never found such great faith even in Israel."
I tell you that many will come from east and west, and sit at table in the kingdom of heaven with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.
But those who should have been heirs to the kingdom will be thrown outside in the dark; there men will weep and gnash their teeth!
Then Jesus said to the centurion, "Go; your servant will be healed because you believed." And at that moment his servant was cured. "He carried our diseases"
When Jesus came to Peter's house, he saw that Peter's mother-in-law was lying in bed with a high fever.
Jesus touched her hand; she got up at once and began to wait on him.
That evening people brought to him many who were possessed by demons; he cast out the spirits with his word and cured all the sick.
This happened so that what was spoken by God through Isaiah would be fulfilled: "He took our illnesses and carried our diseases." Jesus' followers
When Jesus saw large crowds around him, he ordered his disciples to go across the lake.
One of his disciples came to him and said, "Master, I will follow you wherever you go."
Jesus replied, "Foxes have dens to live in, and birds have nests, but the Son of Man has no place even to lay his head."
وقال له تلميذ آخر من تلاميذه: "يا رب، سمحلي إني استنى لحد ما أدفن أبويا."
But Jesus said to him, "Follow me, and let the dead bury their own dead." Jesus calms the storm
Jesus got in the boat, and his disciples followed him.
Then a strong storm came up on the lake, so that the boat was being swamped by waves; but he was sleeping.
They came to him and woke him up, saying, "Master, we're going down! We're perishing!"
Jesus said to them, "Why are you afraid, you men of little faith?" Then he got up and rebuked the winds and the waves, and it was completely calm.
They were amazed and asked, "Who is this? Even the winds and waves obey him!" Jesus drives evil spirits from two men
Then Jesus went over to the other side of the lake, where he was met by two men from the tombs who were possessed with evil spirits. These men were so dangerous that no one dared travel that way.
The evil spirits cried out: "What do you want from us, Son of God? Have you come here to torment us before our appointed time?"
And there was a large herd of pigs grazing at some distance from them.
The evil spirits begged him to let them go, saying, "If you drive us out, send us into the herd of pigs."
Jesus said to them, "Go!" So they came out and went into the pigs, and the whole herd rushed down the steep bank into the lake and were drowned.
The shepherds ran to town and told people what happened to those possessed by evil spirits.
So all the people in the town came out to see Jesus; and when they saw him, they begged him to leave their neighborhood.
Jesus heals a paralyzed man
Jesus got in a boat to cross over to the other side of the lake, and he arrived at his own town.
So some people brought to him a paralyzed man lying on his bed. When Jesus saw their faith, he said to the paralytic, "Take courage, son; your sins are forgiven."
Some religious scholars said: "This man is insulting God with his words."
Jesus knew what they were thinking and said to them, "Why do you have evil thoughts in your hearts?"
Which is easier to say: "Your sins are forgiven" or "Get up and walk"?
But I will show you that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins.” So he said to the man, “Get up, take your mat and go home.”
So he got up and went home.
When people saw this, they were terrified and praised God for giving such authority to human beings. When will Jesus follow?
As Jesus was walking along, he saw a man named Matthew sitting at his tax collection booth. So Jesus said to him, "Follow me!" And Matthew got up and followed him.
While he was eating in Matthew's house, many tax collectors and sinners came and ate with Jesus and his disciples.
When the Pharisees saw this, they asked his disciples, "Why does your teacher eat with tax collectors and sinners?"
When Jesus heard this, he said, "Healthy people don't need a doctor—sick people do."
